# iNiR 2.33 ONLY. Does not apply to 3.x (iRiS moved into a Hub plugin, the shader was rewritten). Kept for reference;
# on 3.x the stock look is kept on purpose and only iris-visualizer.patch is reapplied.
# Local iRiS patches (apply to the runtime copy, then restart):
#   F=~/.config/quickshell/inir/modules/iris/field
#   patch -d ~/.config/quickshell/inir -p1 < ~/dotfiles/inir-dots/patches/iris-glass.patch \
#     && /usr/lib/qt6/bin/qsb --glsl "100 es,120,150" --hlsl 50 --msl 12 -o $F/IrisField.frag.qsb $F/IrisField.frag \
#     && inir restart
# - iris.appearance.glass.exactTint: keep the chosen glass tint (no automatic legibility floor).
# - iris.bar.glassColour / iris.bar.glassTint: the bar's own glass colour and opacity ("" / -1 = follow the theme).
# - The bar's music visualizer stops while the bar is tucked away (it kept the GPU busy while hidden).
# - Field shader (IrisField.frag, recompiled to .qsb as above): same pixels, about 2.5x less GPU. Pixels nothing reaches
#   return early, the shadow skips where it can't show, and no per-body tables (Mesa spilled them to scratch on the
#   Intel UHD: Mod+Space's spotlight opened at ~16 fps). IrisField.qml passes the shape count in options.y.
